{"kind":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The 10 rules that shape every Swidux app, and the reasoning behind them."}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"Related-Documentation","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/ArchitectureGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/BuildingYourFirstApp"],"title":"Related Documentation"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/ArchitectureGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/SecurityPosture"],"anchor":"Explanation","generated":true,"title":"Explanation"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/swidux\/designprinciples"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Article","title":"Design Principles","role":"article","modules":[{"name":"Swidux"}]},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux"],["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/SecurityPosture"]]},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/DesignPrinciples","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Swidux’s surface area looks small — a "},{"code":"Store","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", a reducer protocol, a plugin protocol — but the API is opinionated. These principles explain ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"why"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" the API has the shape it does, so you can extend it correctly.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"1. State is a value, observation is a class","anchor":"1-State-is-a-value-observation-is-a-class","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"State is a struct. Mutations go through ","type":"text"},{"code":"inout State","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", which is predictable, snapshottable, and testable. SwiftUI observation needs an "},{"code":"@Observable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" reference type. Reconciling these two requires a class that mirrors the struct."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Swidux"},{"text":" generates that class for you (","type":"text"},{"code":"<StructName>Observer","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":") and wires up the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxObservable"},{"type":"text","text":" conformance that bridges the two. Don’t hand-write the observer. The "},{"code":"pack → reduce → unpack-diff → observe","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" cycle is what gives you per-property re-renders without coupling reducers to a class."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"@Slice","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" extends this to nested struct slices: each slice gets its own observer class so observation stays granular even across composition."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"anchor":"2-Reducers-are-pure-and-synchronous","type":"heading","text":"2. Reducers are pure and synchronous"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Reducers take ","type":"text"},{"code":"inout State","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and an ","type":"text"},{"code":"Action","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", mutate state in place, and return an optional ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Effect","type":"reference"},{"text":". They never ","type":"text"},{"code":"await","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", never ","type":"text"},{"code":"throw","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and never call I\/O directly.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Why: pure synchronous mutations are trivially testable, deterministic, and snapshot-friendly. When you need async work (network, disk, timers), return an "},{"code":"Effect","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" containing a "},{"code":"@Sendable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" async operation that runs off the MainActor and dispatches follow-up actions back through "},{"code":"send","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"text":"3. Effects run off MainActor; sends hop back","anchor":"3-Effects-run-off-MainActor-sends-hop-back","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Effect","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" is a ","type":"text"},{"code":"Sendable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" value containing an async throwing operation and cancellation metadata. Construct it with ","type":"text"},{"code":"Effect { send in ... }","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"; use ","type":"text"},{"code":"map","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" to lift its actions without losing metadata. The ","type":"text"},{"code":"Store","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" runs effects in ","type":"text"},{"code":"Task { @concurrent in }","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" so they don’t block UI. ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Send","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"code":"@MainActor @Sendable (Action) -> Void","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so dispatching from inside an effect always lands back on MainActor — no manual hops, no race conditions on state.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The split is deliberate: effects own the work, the reducer owns the state.","type":"text"}]},{"anchor":"4-Persistence-is-invisible","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"4. Persistence is invisible"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Reducers mutate ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","type":"reference"},{"text":" properties; ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","type":"reference"},{"text":" records every change in a ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/ChangeSet","type":"reference"},{"text":"; ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","type":"reference"},{"text":" debounces and drains those changesets through ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/StateWriter","type":"reference"},{"text":" closures.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"You never write ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"db.save()"},{"text":" in a feature. A reducer that adds an item is identical whether the entity is persisted to SwiftData, SQLite, or nowhere — register or don’t register a writer. This is the principle that makes Swidux apps feel small: persistence stops being a concern of feature code.","type":"text"}]},{"anchor":"5-Synchronous-state-async-persistence","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"5. Synchronous state, async persistence"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"State updates synchronously inside the reducer for instant UI feedback. Persistence happens asynchronously: ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","type":"reference"},{"text":" change tracking is in-memory and free; the debounced persistence flush coalesces rapid mutations into a single batched write.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Tap-tap-tap-tap on an increment button updates the UI on every tap and produces one DB write a moment later. Reducers stay synchronous; storage stays cheap.","type":"text"}]},{"anchor":"6-Plugins-are-the-single-extension-point","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"6. Plugins are the single extension point"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Everything that hangs off the dispatch cycle is a ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/SwiduxPlugin","type":"reference"},{"text":". Persistence, undo, killswitch, parental gate, paywall — same protocol, same lifecycle hooks. You can add your own without forking Swidux.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Two structural patterns:","type":"text"}]},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Core plugins","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" (","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin"},{"text":") — action-agnostic. Doesn’t know your action type. Couples only to state shape (","type":"text"},{"code":"Equatable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for undo; ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore"},{"type":"text","text":" keypaths for persistence)."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Domain plugins","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" (","type":"text"},{"code":"KillswitchPlugin","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"ParentalGatePlugin","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"PaywallPlugin","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", your own) — owns a state slice and an action enum. Wires into your root types via keypath + action lifter + extractor.","type":"text"}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The decision rule: "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"does this need to know your action type?","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" If no, write a core plugin and use "},{"code":"willReduce","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"code":"afterReduce","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". If yes, write a domain plugin and use ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reduce"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"level":2,"anchor":"7-Bind-to-the-store-not-to-State","type":"heading","text":"7. Bind to the store, not to `@State`"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Form inputs read from the store and dispatch on write. Use ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store\/binding(_:sending:)"},{"text":" for the common case (read one property, dispatch one action), and fall back to ","type":"text"},{"code":"Binding(get:set:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" when the read is a transformation (optional unwraps, derived values) or the setter wraps the dispatch in animation or branching. Don’t buffer mutable form state in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@State"},{"text":" and write back on a button.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Why: every mutation flows through the reducer, which means undo\/redo, persistence, and any plugin that watches the dispatch cycle sees every keystroke (subject to coalescing). If you stash state in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@State"},{"text":", those plugins are blind to it.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The trade-off is more dispatches per keystroke. Coalescing — see ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin"},{"text":" — collapses bursts of the same action into a single undo step.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"8. Registration order matters at the boundaries","level":2,"anchor":"8-Registration-order-matters-at-the-boundaries","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" snapshots in "},{"code":"willReduce","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", so it must run "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"before"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" any plugin or reducer mutates state — register it first. "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" drains changelogs in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"afterReduce"},{"type":"text","text":", so it wants the post-mutation state — register it after undo. Domain plugins use only "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reduce"},{"type":"text","text":", so their relative order rarely matters."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The recommended order:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["plugins.register(undoPlugin)         \/\/ 1. snapshots first","plugins.register(persistencePlugin)  \/\/ 2. drains after reducer","plugins.register(killswitchPlugin)   \/\/ 3. domain plugins","plugins.register(paywallPlugin)","plugins.register(parentalGatePlugin)"],"syntax":"swift"},{"anchor":"9-Strict-concurrency-on-purpose","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"9. Strict concurrency, on purpose"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Swidux is built for ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"swiftLanguageMode(.v6)"},{"text":" and assumes Swift 6 strict concurrency throughout. State must be ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sendable"},{"type":"text","text":". The macros mark generated code carefully. Effects use explicit isolation ("},{"code":"@Sendable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"@MainActor","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"@concurrent","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":")."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This is friction at first — you’ll get warnings about "},{"code":"Sendable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" types. Honour them. The result is a state-management layer that composes safely with "},{"code":"async\/await","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and SwiftData without the surprise data races you get from pre-Swift 6 designs."}]},{"anchor":"10-The-store-is-opinionated-your-app-is-not","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"10. The store is opinionated; your app is not"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Swidux gives you a ","type":"text"},{"code":"Store","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", a reducer protocol, a plugin protocol, and three optional plugins. It does not give you:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A dependency-injection container (write your own ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AppEnvironment"},{"text":").","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A navigation library (use SwiftUI navigation).","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A network layer (use ","type":"text"},{"code":"URLSession","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", structured concurrency, or whatever you want).","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An opinion on database (SwiftData, GRDB, SQLite, Core Data — register a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"StateWriter"},{"type":"text","text":" and Swidux doesn’t care)."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The store owns one job: take an action, produce a new state, run effects. Everything else is yours.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"11-Service-shapes-protocol-when-others-implement-it-closures-when-we-own-it","text":"11. Service shapes: protocol when others implement it, closures when we own it","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Swidux services deliberately come in two shapes, chosen by who supplies the implementation:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Protocol"}]},{"text":" — when apps or vendor adapters implement the backend:","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PaywallService"},{"text":" (RevenueCat, StoreKit, simulated), ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AnalyticsService"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(Mixpanel, Amplitude, console), ","type":"text"},{"code":"FeatureFlagsService","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (any JSON host).","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"A protocol gives conformers a stable, documented contract.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Struct of closures","type":"text"}]},{"text":" — when the library owns the shape and apps only","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"configure or mock it: ","type":"text"},{"code":"KillswitchService","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ParentalChallengeSource"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SyncPreflightService"},{"text":". Closures make the built-in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".live"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".mock"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"factories and per-test overrides trivial without a conformance ceremony.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The split is a signal, not an accident: if you find yourself conforming to a","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"struct-of-closures service, that service was designed to be configured, not","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"replaced.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Anti-patterns","anchor":"Anti-patterns"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"❌ "},{"code":"await","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"try"},{"type":"text","text":" inside a reducer — return an effect instead."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"❌ Hand-writing the observer class when you could use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Swidux"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"❌ Calling ","type":"text"},{"code":"db.save()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" from inside a reducer — use ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/StateWriter","type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"❌ Mutating state from inside an effect — effects dispatch actions; the reducer mutates.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"❌ Owning the store with ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@StateObject"},{"text":" — use ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@State"},{"text":" (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Store"},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Observable"},{"text":", not ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ObservableObject"},{"text":").","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"❌ Buffering form state in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@State"},{"type":"text","text":" and committing on submit — bind to the store directly."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"❌ Registering ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin"},{"text":" before ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","type":"reference"},{"text":" — snapshot must precede mutation.","type":"text"}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"}]}],"sections":[],"references":{"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/SecurityPosture":{"role":"collectionGroup","kind":"article","title":"Security Posture","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/SecurityPosture","abstract":[{"text":"What Swidux’s soft controls actually guarantee, and what to do when you need a hard one.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/securityposture","type":"topic"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/Send":{"role":"symbol","title":"Send","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"typealias"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Send"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Send"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Send","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Dispatches an action back to the store from an effect."}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/send","type":"topic"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/Store/binding(_:sending:)":{"title":"binding(_:sending:)","abstract":[{"text":"Creates a SwiftUI ","type":"text"},{"code":"Binding","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" that reads a property through the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"observer tree and dispatches an action when written.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"binding"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Value"},{"kind":"text","text":">("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:s7KeyPathC","text":"KeyPath"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"State"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:6Swidux0A10ObservableP8ObserverQa","text":"Observer"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Value"},{"kind":"text","text":">, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"sending"},{"kind":"text","text":": ("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Value"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"text":"Action","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7SwiftUI7BindingV","text":"Binding","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Value","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store\/binding(_:sending:)","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","conformance":{"conformancePrefix":[{"type":"text","text":"Conforms when"}],"availabilityPrefix":[{"type":"text","text":"Available when"}],"constraints":[{"code":"State","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" conforms to "},{"code":"SwiduxObservable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/store\/binding(_:sending:)","type":"topic"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/ArchitectureGuide":{"role":"article","kind":"article","title":"Architecture & Performance","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/ArchitectureGuide","abstract":[{"text":"Understand the architectural patterns that make Swidux work correctly with SwiftUI’s observation system.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/architectureguide","type":"topic"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PluginArchitecture":{"role":"article","kind":"article","title":"Plugin Architecture","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture","abstract":[{"text":"Extend the dispatch cycle with lifecycle hooks — from invisible infrastructure to domain-specific features.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginarchitecture","type":"topic"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/ChangeSet":{"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","title":"ChangeSet","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ChangeSet"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"ChangeSet"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/ChangeSet","abstract":[{"text":"Tracks which entity IDs have been created\/updated or deleted.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/changeset","type":"topic"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PersistencePlugin":{"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/persistenceplugin","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Coalescing persistence plugin."}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"PersistencePlugin","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"PersistencePlugin","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"PersistencePlugin"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/UndoPlugin":{"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","title":"UndoPlugin","fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"UndoPlugin","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"UndoPlugin","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Snapshot-based undo\/redo plugin."}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/undoplugin","type":"topic"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/BuildingYourFirstApp":{"role":"article","kind":"article","title":"Build Your First Swidux App","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/BuildingYourFirstApp","abstract":[{"text":"Build a counter app from scratch and meet the four moving parts of a Swidux project: state, action, reducer, and store.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/buildingyourfirstapp","type":"topic"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/StateWriter":{"fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"StateWriter","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"Accumulates entity snapshots and produces batched async persistence work.","type":"text"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"StateWriter","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/StateWriter","type":"topic","title":"StateWriter","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/statewriter"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/EntityStore":{"role":"symbol","title":"EntityStore","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"EntityStore"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"EntityStore"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","abstract":[{"text":"An ordered, keyed collection of identifiable entities that silently records","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"every mutation for downstream persistence.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/entitystore","type":"topic"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux","kind":"symbol","title":"Swidux","abstract":[{"text":"Redux-style state management for SwiftUI, with macros for observability and ready-made plugins for persistence, undo, paywalls, version killswitches, and parental gates.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux","type":"topic","role":"collection"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/SwiduxPlugin":{"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/swiduxplugin","fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SwiduxPlugin","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/SwiduxPlugin","title":"SwiduxPlugin","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A plugin that participates in the Swidux dispatch cycle."}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"SwiduxPlugin","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/Effect":{"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","title":"Effect","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Effect"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Effect"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Effect","abstract":[{"text":"Async work with cancellation metadata declared before the store starts it.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/effect","type":"topic"}}}